# CRITICAL HARDWARE CONSTRAINT — READ THIS FIRST

The development machine has **16 GB system RAM**.

The laptop has already experienced a system-level memory-overuse problem during previous RAG experimentation.

Therefore, **memory safety is a hard engineering requirement for this task.**

DO NOT implement the entire proposed retrieval architecture as one large memory-heavy operation.

Do NOT simultaneously:

* load the complete medical corpus into RAM
* rebuild the Qdrant index
* generate embeddings for the entire corpus
* construct a full in-memory BM25 index
* retrieve Top-100 candidates for multiple queries
* run a cross-encoder over all candidates
* execute multiple patient cases
* run the complete regression suite

in the same process or at the same time.

The retrieval redesign MUST be implemented incrementally.

The existing Qdrant medical index should be reused whenever possible.

