dense_candidate_k = 20
bm25_candidate_k = 20
reranker_candidate_k = 20
final_evidence_k = 5
```

Do NOT start with Top-100.

Do NOT increase candidate counts until the smaller configuration has been tested successfully.

Process one patient case at a time.

Process retrieval queries sequentially rather than concurrently.

Do not create unnecessary copies of candidate lists, embeddings, documents, or corpus text.

Release temporary objects after each retrieval stage where practical.

Do not keep dense candidates, BM25 candidates, reranker tensors, and full corpus representations in memory simultaneously unless strictly necessary.

If a component requires substantial additional RAM, measure or estimate its memory requirements before enabling it.

If memory usage becomes unsafe, STOP the experiment rather than continuing automatically.

