# 7. REMOVE THE CURRENT HARD PRE-RERANK FILTER

The existing:

```text
filter_candidates()
```

currently retains candidates based on:

1. title overlap with symptom/history concepts

OR

2. at least two symptom concepts appearing in the candidate text.

Candidates failing both are rejected.

Do NOT allow this rule to eliminate candidates before broader ranking.

It is too aggressive as a candidate-generation gate.

Instead, concept overlap should become a ranking feature.

For example:

```text
semantic relevance
+
lexical relevance
+
concept overlap
+
history relevance
+
demographic relevance
+
source quality
```

should contribute to final ranking.

Concept overlap should NOT be a binary:

```text
pass / reject
```

gate at the early stage.

During Phase 1, if `filter_candidates()` must remain temporarily present for compatibility, modify it carefully so that diagnostic/safety behavior is not broken, but do not use it to prematurely discard potentially useful retrieval candidates.

