Only after Phase 1 has been tested successfully should BM25 be introduced.

Do NOT immediately load the entire corpus into an oversized in-memory BM25 structure.

First inspect how the current medical corpus/index is represented.

Prefer an implementation that:

* avoids unnecessary corpus duplication
* processes data efficiently
* does not create multiple copies of the same text
* limits candidate output to Top-20
* does not retain unnecessary intermediate data

If building a persistent BM25 index is appropriate, build it as a separate one-time indexing step rather than rebuilding it every time the application starts.

Do not rebuild it during every demo execution.

