# 13. FINAL EVIDENCE SELECTION

After ranking, select a small final set.

Target:

```text
3–5 useful passages
```

Do NOT force exactly five if only two passages are genuinely useful.

Do NOT fill the final evidence set with weak or redundant passages merely to reach five.

Prefer complementary evidence.

---

# 14. THE SYSTEM MUST NOT DIAGNOSE FROM RETRIEVAL

This distinction must remain explicit.

Retrieving:

```text
Asthma information
```

does NOT mean:

```text
Patient has asthma.
```

Retrieving:

```text
Panic attack information
```

does NOT mean:

```text
Patient has a panic attack.
```

Retrieval only provides medical knowledge that the downstream diagnostic agent may use as evidence.

The diagnostic agent remains responsible for uncertainty and hypothesis generation.

